.RE
.P
These constants are additionally supported on the SPARC architecture:
.RS
.TP 
\fBB76800\fP
.TQ
\fBB153600\fP
.TQ
\fBB307200\fP
.TQ
\fBB614400\fP
.RE
.P
These constants are additionally supported on non\-SPARC architectures:
.RS
.TP 
\fBB2500000\fP
.TQ
\fBB3000000\fP
.TQ
\fBB3500000\fP
.TQ
\fBB4000000\fP
.RE
.P
Due to differences between architectures, portable applications should check
if a particular \fBB\fP\fInnn\fP constant is defined prior to using it.
.P
The zero baud rate, \fBB0\fP, is used to terminate the connection.  If \fBB0\fP is
specified, the modem control lines shall no longer be asserted.  Normally,
this will disconnect the line.  \fBCBAUDEX\fP is a mask for the speeds beyond
those defined in POSIX.1 (57600 and above).  Thus, \fBB57600\fP & \fBCBAUDEX\fP is
nonzero.
.P
Setting the baud rate to a value other than those defined by \fBB\fP\fInnn\fP
constants is possible via the \fBTCSETS2\fP ioctl; see \fBioctl_tty\fP(2).
.P
\fBcfgetispeed\fP()  は \fItermios\fP 構造体中の入力ボーレートを返す。
.P
\fBcfsetispeed\fP()  sets the input baud rate stored in the \fItermios\fP
structure to \fIspeed\fP, which must be specified as one of the \fBB\fP\fInnn\fP
constants listed above for \fBcfsetospeed\fP().  If the input baud rate is set
to the literal constant \fB0\fP (not the symbolic constant \fBB0\fP), the input
baud rate will be equal to the output baud rate.
.P
\fBcfsetspeed\fP()  は 4.4BSD による拡張である。この関数は \fBcfsetispeed\fP()
と同じ引数をとり、入出力両方の速度を設定する。
.SH 返り値
\fBcfgetispeed\fP()  は \fItermios\fP 構造体中の入力ボーレートを返す。
.P
\fBcfgetospeed\fP()  は \fItermios\fP 構造体中の出力ボーレートを返す。
.P
他のすべての関数の戻り値:
.TP 
\fB0\fP
実行成功。
.TP 
\fB\-1\fP
実行失敗。 \fIerrno\fP がエラーの種類を示す。
.P
Note that \fBtcsetattr\fP()  returns success if \fIany\fP of the requested changes
could be successfully carried out.  Therefore, when making multiple changes,
it may be necessary to follow this call with a further call to
\fBtcgetattr\fP()  to check that all changes have been performed successfully.
